      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Battle of Plassey (1757)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Battle of Plassey (1757) initiated the foundation of British rule in India.",
        "The Battle of Buxar (1764) consolidated British political control over Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa.",
        "The Treaty of Allahabad (1765) granted Diwani rights (revenue collection) to the East India Company.",
        "Territorial annexation was systematically accelerated using policies like the Subsidiary Alliance and Doctrine of Lapse.",
        "British expansion severely impacted the traditional Indian economic structure and governance."
      ],
      "id": "q5tyazi"
    },
